 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? Make sure his room is familiar and easy to navigate, with everything within reach. Avoid his chair and TV remote, if possible. Then keep things simple. A picture list of daily routines can help. Yes, new places can be very upsetting. Plan ahead and keep him near you wherever possible. If he's comfortable doing so, little outings can be good. Keep them short and don't be disappointed if he doesn't remember much. That' understandable. Having support can make a huge difference. Maybe bring along a family member who can help.",
